  "family_guidance": "# Mosaic R14 task supplement\n\nRead the assigned case's task.json and target-pattern.png. Numeric geometry and\ncompletion conditions live in that task file; use its actual robot bases,\nworkspace, cameras and target dimensions. The named Mosaic skill applies to\nplacement, release and collaboration. The assigned role and shared robot tool\ncontract govern execution.\n\nThe supplied pattern matrix and image already have their final world\norientation: row 1 is north (+Y), column 1 is west (−X). Use the supplied\nreference as-is. Background-colored cells are part of the artwork.\n\nEvery cell needs a distinct released cube of its required color. Source labels\ndescribe initial inventory and do not establish exclusive ownership. Supplies\ncontain mixed colors to support nearby placements; inspect the current RGB and\nchoose useful local work as well as needed cross-zone access, staging or\nhandovers. There is no prescribed allocation, local percentage, color order or\ntransfer route. Compare total handling, reach, congestion and concurrent work.\n\nL1 uses real recessed pockets; L2 printed lines are visual marks; L3 has no\nvisible grid, with the same declared assembly frame. Placement, release and\nwithdrawal are separate events. Later contact may disturb a completed cell;\ninspect affected results again and preserve verified work while enabling\nindependent work with full-arm, payload and opening-finger clearance.\n\nTrack objects through permitted timestamped RGB and robot/action feedback.\nPublic target coordinates and a commanded TCP do not measure an object's actual\npose. This supplement contains no precomputed action sequence or Oracle\nexperience. Choose and revise motion from current allowed evidence.\n",
